  the hand, pinched corner-first between the curved proximal links and tilted ~15
  deg, with the pads splayed below it touching nothing. Textbook wedge, and it
  explains all four run-1 symptoms at once: blocked 17 mm wide, zero pad force,
  a 10 mm settle on release, then a rigid ride through the lift.
